WEBVTT

00:00:01.280 --> 00:00:04.370
<i>This is the second son of 
a mold-starter business</i>

00:00:04.370 --> 00:00:06.480
<i>who just started at the Agricultural 
University this spring,</i>

00:00:06.480 --> 00:00:08.980
<i>Sawaki Souemon Tadayasu-kun.</i>

00:00:09.440 --> 00:00:13.620
<i>He has the ability to see 
microbes with the naked eye.</i>

00:00:13.620 --> 00:00:14.990
<i>Amazing, isn't it?</i>

00:01:39.470 --> 00:01:41.710
Can you tell where they're 
coming from, Sawaki?

00:01:43.200 --> 00:01:44.370
There, Kei!

00:01:45.100 --> 00:01:46.870
Hiochi are pouring out of that window!

00:01:47.500 --> 00:01:49.070
There are so many...

00:02:01.530 --> 00:02:04.470
The 300 Million Yen Agricultural 
University Student

00:02:10.000 --> 00:02:12.970
Doesn't this seem off somehow?

00:02:12.970 --> 00:02:14.510
Let's see...

00:02:15.650 --> 00:02:17.510
It looks fine.

00:02:17.510 --> 00:02:20.450
It's the smell. Doesn't it smell weird?

00:02:20.450 --> 00:02:21.440
Does it?

00:02:26.620 --> 00:02:28.370
Hiochi Bacteria

00:02:29.820 --> 00:02:32.390
Those hiochi are really 
flying out of there.

00:02:32.390 --> 00:02:34.350
Why would there be hiochi here?

00:02:34.350 --> 00:02:35.750
That is strange.

00:02:36.310 --> 00:02:37.730
This building is too old.

00:02:37.730 --> 00:02:40.530
So it's only being used for 
Professor Itsuki's lab

00:02:40.530 --> 00:02:42.090
and some storage rooms.

00:02:42.090 --> 00:02:43.840
But there appear to be some

00:02:43.840 --> 00:02:46.440
students using those storage 
rooms for themselves.

00:02:49.180 --> 00:02:52.440
Japanese 
Sake

00:02:49.630 --> 00:02:52.170
Looks like the floor is about 
to collapse here, too.

00:02:52.170 --> 00:02:53.440
No use worrying about that now.

00:02:53.690 --> 00:02:56.030
The floor's collapsing 
all over the place here.

00:02:56.030 --> 00:02:57.980
I know, but...

00:02:58.920 --> 00:03:02.570
Is it okay to make sake in a place 
where the floor is so weak?

00:03:02.990 --> 00:03:04.620
Hey, don't walk there!

00:03:04.620 --> 00:03:05.950
You're rocking the tank!

00:03:08.870 --> 00:03:09.500
Whoa!

00:03:19.410 --> 00:03:20.800
What was that?!

00:03:23.350 --> 00:03:24.700
There are more flying out!

00:03:24.700 --> 00:03:25.850
It's a hiochi party!

00:03:26.750 --> 00:03:28.580
When you say "hiochi,"

00:03:28.580 --> 00:03:31.420
you mean the hiochi 
bacteria that ruin sake?

00:03:31.420 --> 00:03:32.230
Yes!

00:03:34.200 --> 00:03:37.380
Hiochi bacteria, a type 
of lactic acid bacteria,

00:03:37.380 --> 00:03:39.070
primarily feed on the mevalonic acids

00:03:39.070 --> 00:03:41.480
that malt fungi produce,

00:03:41.480 --> 00:03:43.340
so they can cause a sort of disease

00:03:43.340 --> 00:03:46.240
characteristic to sake made 
from those malt fungi.

00:03:47.300 --> 00:03:51.500
Yuuki-kun, I'm sure it's a bacteria 
that you hate intensely.

00:03:52.250 --> 00:03:53.460
Hiochi are...

00:03:54.710 --> 00:03:56.250
my enemy.

00:03:56.590 --> 00:03:59.710
Yuuki Liquors

00:03:58.590 --> 00:03:59.710
Chief!

00:04:00.040 --> 00:04:01.200
You fool!

00:04:01.200 --> 00:04:04.110
How could you do this over 
a thing like hiochi?!

00:04:04.110 --> 00:04:06.970
All of the tanks were ruined?

00:04:07.490 --> 00:04:08.750
Grab that side.

00:04:08.750 --> 00:04:10.350
Lower him slowly.

00:04:11.450 --> 00:04:15.100
Tadayasu, Kei... come outside with me.

00:04:19.450 --> 00:04:21.990
Hiochi led our chief 
brewer to kill himself,

00:04:22.880 --> 00:04:25.490
and nearly ruined our brewery.

00:04:26.390 --> 00:04:29.830
And if large quantities of hiochi 
are occurring, that means...

00:04:29.830 --> 00:04:33.000
Someone might be illicitly 
making sake downstairs.

00:04:33.390 --> 00:04:34.370
Illicitly?

00:04:34.900 --> 00:04:35.840
Let's go.

00:04:36.410 --> 00:04:38.500
Let's go with them, Sawaki!

00:04:38.500 --> 00:04:39.900
Why?

00:04:39.900 --> 00:04:41.370
You're a brewer's son.

00:04:41.370 --> 00:04:42.600
You don't want to see that, do you?

00:04:42.600 --> 00:04:43.690
No...

00:04:43.690 --> 00:04:46.260
I just can't ignore hiochi!

00:04:58.060 --> 00:05:00.150
Sawaki! Where are the hiochi?

00:05:00.560 --> 00:05:02.980
Uh... everywhere.

00:05:02.980 --> 00:05:04.220
Which room?

00:05:04.220 --> 00:05:06.090
If someone is making 
sake without permission,

00:05:06.090 --> 00:05:07.230
it's a huge problem!

00:05:07.230 --> 00:05:08.780
A crime, even!

00:05:08.780 --> 00:05:11.420
Sawaki, figure out 
which room they're in!

00:05:13.150 --> 00:05:14.150
Get going!

00:05:14.630 --> 00:05:15.870
What am I, a dog?

00:05:16.950 --> 00:05:19.630
Jeez, there are so many of them.

00:05:20.120 --> 00:05:21.700
Disgusting...

00:05:21.700 --> 00:05:23.630
Hell, I can't even see in front of me.

00:05:24.390 --> 00:05:26.900
Hurry it up! You're not even moving!

00:05:26.900 --> 00:05:28.550
You just don't get it.

00:05:31.960 --> 00:05:33.120
This is it.

00:05:33.120 --> 00:05:34.400
They're coming from this door.

00:05:34.400 --> 00:05:35.060
Here?!

00:05:46.360 --> 00:05:47.740
This tank...

00:05:47.740 --> 00:05:49.680
It's sake, all right.

00:05:49.680 --> 00:05:51.280
What on earth happened?

00:05:51.280 --> 00:05:53.580
So someone really was 
serious about making sake.

00:05:53.580 --> 00:05:55.000
You call this serious?

00:05:55.560 --> 00:05:58.420
You can't make sake in an 
environment like this!

00:05:58.420 --> 00:05:59.750
The floor is rotting.

00:06:00.060 --> 00:06:02.750
Looks like it couldn't bear 
the weight of the tank.

00:06:03.430 --> 00:06:05.570
Still, no one could produce a whole tank

00:06:05.570 --> 00:06:07.380
of spoiled sake in a laboratory.

00:06:07.820 --> 00:06:10.940
This could make for a 
valuable sample in itself.

00:06:11.410 --> 00:06:13.420
Where are the hiochi gathering?

00:06:14.500 --> 00:06:17.000
Well... they're all over the room.

00:06:17.000 --> 00:06:17.890
Sawaki...

00:06:18.560 --> 00:06:21.220
Let's borrow a burner and 
fry those hiochi to death!

00:06:21.220 --> 00:06:22.350
Whoa, whoa...

00:06:22.350 --> 00:06:25.000
Wait, did he just say Sawaki?

00:06:26.510 --> 00:06:29.540
Professor, do you have some 
ethanol or something?

00:06:29.540 --> 00:06:31.850
I'll throw it around and kill 
every last one of those—

00:06:40.230 --> 00:06:44.170
In the past, sake ruined by hiochi 
was restored using ashes.

00:06:45.270 --> 00:06:46.160
What?

00:06:46.160 --> 00:06:50.880
Adding alkaline wood 
ashes to acidic sake

00:06:50.880 --> 00:06:54.530
neutralized it and 
eliminated the hiochi.

00:06:54.970 --> 00:06:56.930
The effects of ash as a preservative have

00:06:56.930 --> 00:06:59.640
been well-known in Japan for a long time.

00:07:00.230 --> 00:07:02.650
Sawaki-kun, your family's 
business uses ashes

00:07:02.650 --> 00:07:06.360
to raise pure cultures of 
malt fungi, does it not?

00:07:07.200 --> 00:07:10.220
The use of ashes could 
be called the precursor

00:07:10.220 --> 00:07:12.240
to modern bio-science in Japan.

00:07:12.790 --> 00:07:14.550
Nowadays, the power of science allows us

00:07:14.550 --> 00:07:16.880
to prevent infestations to some extent,

00:07:16.880 --> 00:07:20.120
but hiochi bacteria will forever 
be the sake brewer's worst enemy.

00:07:20.930 --> 00:07:24.570
I can understand why Yuuki-kun 
hates them so much.

00:07:24.570 --> 00:07:26.760
Um, is there anything we can wipe off—

00:07:26.760 --> 00:07:27.620
No.

00:07:29.600 --> 00:07:32.800
Well, I'm going to get back to my research.

00:07:32.800 --> 00:07:34.480
Take care of the rest, okay?

00:07:36.700 --> 00:07:39.710
I think looking for the 
culprit is more important.

00:07:40.260 --> 00:07:41.600
I'll leave this mess to you.

00:07:43.470 --> 00:07:45.650
What's with these people?

00:07:45.930 --> 00:07:49.150
But the hiochi really 
do seem to be gone.

00:07:49.930 --> 00:07:51.360
Hey, Kei...

00:07:51.360 --> 00:07:52.780
Let's head back, too.

00:07:53.220 --> 00:07:56.280
No. You wipe up the sake on the floor.

00:07:56.970 --> 00:07:59.350
I'll kill the hiochi.

00:08:01.160 --> 00:08:03.230
Kill... Kill...

00:08:02.220 --> 00:08:04.140
Um... Kei?

00:08:04.140 --> 00:08:08.020
Kill... Kill... Kill...

00:08:06.450 --> 00:08:08.020
I thought I was gonna die.

00:08:08.020 --> 00:08:11.030
This is the work of Itsuki and Hasegawa.

00:08:12.050 --> 00:08:13.890
Are you the ones behind 
the illicit brewing?

00:08:14.660 --> 00:08:17.630
Oh... don't worry about that.

00:08:18.260 --> 00:08:21.270
You're both in suits... 
so you guys are new students?

00:08:21.270 --> 00:08:22.770
Y-Yeah...

00:08:23.580 --> 00:08:26.150
And... how did you know it was hiochi?

00:08:26.730 --> 00:08:30.530
Well... his parents own a brewery, so...

00:08:34.680 --> 00:08:38.140
Oh, yeah! You guys should 
come to our dorm.

00:08:38.140 --> 00:08:39.690
It's on campus.

00:08:39.690 --> 00:08:43.440
Yeah! You can't go back without 
taking a shower, right?

00:08:44.070 --> 00:08:44.920
Yeah...

00:08:45.550 --> 00:08:49.130
Anyway, I never expected to 
end up covered in ashes.

00:08:49.130 --> 00:08:50.920
You can say that again.

00:08:51.640 --> 00:08:53.900
It's often said that sake 
turns into vinegar,

00:08:53.900 --> 00:08:56.480
but it doesn't really.

00:08:56.480 --> 00:08:58.610
People in the old days said that

00:08:58.610 --> 00:09:01.360
because sake infested with hiochi

00:09:01.360 --> 00:09:03.060
turns cloudy and gives 
off a strong smell—

00:09:02.530 --> 00:09:03.510
Hey!

00:09:03.510 --> 00:09:06.430
Aren't they those second-years, 
Misato and Kawahama?

00:09:06.430 --> 00:09:07.400
So it is.

00:09:08.010 --> 00:09:09.470
That Misato Kaoru has been

00:09:09.470 --> 00:09:12.330
popping into my lab a 
lot since last summer,

00:09:12.330 --> 00:09:14.900
trying to learn all he can 
about sake production.

00:09:15.510 --> 00:09:17.290
And Kawahama Takuma seemed more

00:09:17.290 --> 00:09:21.410
interested in biological resources 
and nutrition than in my seminar.

00:09:22.050 --> 00:09:25.090
At any rate, they're idiots 
for trying to illicitly brew

00:09:25.090 --> 00:09:26.200
sake on school grounds!

00:09:26.200 --> 00:09:26.670
Yes...

00:09:27.370 --> 00:09:31.520
And if they try to involve 
Sawaki-kun in their schemes,

00:09:31.520 --> 00:09:33.670
things could get very interesting.

00:09:35.660 --> 00:09:39.180
I accidentally told those 
two the other day...

00:09:40.200 --> 00:09:44.260
that a boy who can see microbes 
was about to enter the school.

00:09:46.560 --> 00:09:47.890
Hiochi Bacteria

00:09:48.690 --> 00:09:49.940
A. oryzae

00:09:52.840 --> 00:09:54.130
We're here.

00:09:54.580 --> 00:09:55.360
This is it.

00:09:56.500 --> 00:09:57.650
Shabby...

00:10:03.890 --> 00:10:05.870
Baths

00:10:03.890 --> 00:10:05.870
In 
Use

00:10:05.010 --> 00:10:05.870
Pre-seminar?

00:10:05.890 --> 00:10:08.440
Agricultural 
University 
Rice Bran 
Shampoo

00:10:06.240 --> 00:10:08.590
Yeah. At this school we

00:10:08.590 --> 00:10:11.430
decide which lab to 
join in the third year.

00:10:11.430 --> 00:10:13.640
It's sort of like a preview of that.

00:10:13.640 --> 00:10:14.630
Oh...

00:10:14.630 --> 00:10:18.410
And, well, Itsuki sort 
of helped us out once...

00:10:18.410 --> 00:10:19.780
just once.

00:10:19.780 --> 00:10:23.720
Why are you talking like this is 
some sort of lazy orientation?

00:10:23.720 --> 00:10:27.300
Oh, and thanks for lending 
us these clothes.

00:10:27.300 --> 00:10:29.900
They're not exactly stylish, 
but it's all we had.

00:10:29.900 --> 00:10:31.110
Try to put up with it.

00:10:34.980 --> 00:10:37.810
Well, Kei, ready to head back?

00:10:37.810 --> 00:10:38.900
Hey, hold on...

00:10:39.390 --> 00:10:41.140
You're Sawaki, right?

00:10:41.140 --> 00:10:43.530
The one they say has 
some strange ability...

00:10:42.890 --> 00:10:46.370
Put the dryer 
back where 
you found it.

00:10:44.640 --> 00:10:46.370
Could we have a little talk?

00:10:46.850 --> 00:10:50.530
We're sort of in a bind 
since that sake was ruined.

00:10:51.080 --> 00:10:55.520
Why were you making sake 
in a place like that?

00:10:56.170 --> 00:11:01.060
A whole tank goes well beyond 
the level of illicit brewing.

00:11:01.060 --> 00:11:03.340
And to let it all go to waste...

00:11:03.870 --> 00:11:06.010
It's like throwing away 
a small fortune.

00:11:06.600 --> 00:11:08.250
It's senseless.

00:11:08.250 --> 00:11:10.690
As the son of a brewery owner, 
I can't even imagine it.

00:11:10.690 --> 00:11:13.120
C-Come on, don't say that...

00:11:13.120 --> 00:11:15.710
We really need money.

00:11:16.750 --> 00:11:19.330
Anyway, let's talk about 
this in our room.

00:11:19.330 --> 00:11:20.900
Yes, please fill us in.

00:11:22.240 --> 00:11:25.730
Kei... I didn't know you liked poking 
your nose into other people's business.

00:11:29.150 --> 00:11:32.730
Oh, you guys are back from 
visiting home already?

00:11:32.730 --> 00:11:33.420
Uh, yeah.

00:11:34.210 --> 00:11:38.120
Sorry for leaving the 
sake all up to you.

00:11:38.120 --> 00:11:41.330
No problem. Leave it to us.

00:11:41.330 --> 00:11:42.700
Well, come on in.

00:11:45.420 --> 00:11:46.820
Pardon the intrusion.

00:11:49.950 --> 00:11:55.940
Geotrichum

00:11:50.760 --> 00:11:53.620
But, what are we gonna do, Misato?

00:11:53.620 --> 00:11:56.420
Relax. We'll think of something.

00:11:55.960 --> 00:12:00.440
A. alternata

00:11:56.420 --> 00:11:58.010
There's nothing to think of.

00:11:58.010 --> 00:12:00.290
We're out of ideas and money.

00:12:00.290 --> 00:12:04.950
I know, but we have to at least 
return the money we borrowed.

00:12:00.690 --> 00:12:04.950
R. javanicus
Geotrichum
M. mucedo
A. niger

00:12:05.280 --> 00:12:08.280
I guess our only choice is to 
sell the stuff in our room.

00:12:08.850 --> 00:12:12.580
You were planning to sell 
the sake you were making?

00:12:12.580 --> 00:12:13.290
Yeah.

00:12:14.090 --> 00:12:17.750
We were going to sell it at our stall 
during the school's spring festival.

00:12:17.750 --> 00:12:21.250
We borrowed money from the 
other guys working the stall,

00:12:21.250 --> 00:12:23.680
and told them we'd get the sake cheap.

00:12:24.430 --> 00:12:27.830
That was the sake made with 
the money they lent us.

00:12:27.830 --> 00:12:29.990
If it had worked, we could have paid off

00:12:29.990 --> 00:12:31.850
our backed up dorm fees, too.

00:12:32.520 --> 00:12:35.600
And that's why we wanted 
to talk to you...

00:12:36.580 --> 00:12:40.080
Can we get some air in here first?

00:12:40.520 --> 00:12:42.990
There's so much mold in 
here, it's not even funny.

00:12:44.540 --> 00:12:45.910
Hey, Sawaki!

00:12:45.910 --> 00:12:48.000
You can see microbes, right?

00:12:48.000 --> 00:12:50.110
Can't you help us make some 
money off of that somehow?

00:12:50.110 --> 00:12:51.560
What are you doing?!

00:12:51.140 --> 00:12:53.000
Please? Come on, Sawaki!

00:12:51.560 --> 00:12:54.960
Like, are there any new 
species of microbes in here?

00:12:54.960 --> 00:12:55.500
Huh?

00:12:55.840 --> 00:12:59.230
No, it doesn't even have 
to be a new species.

00:12:59.230 --> 00:13:01.760
Is there anything we could make money 
off of, like matsutake spores?

00:13:04.080 --> 00:13:08.530
So that's why you invited us here.

00:13:08.530 --> 00:13:11.220
Well, unfortunately, all I see in here

00:13:11.220 --> 00:13:13.760
are the usual black and blue molds.

00:13:13.760 --> 00:13:15.640
No good, huh...

00:13:16.910 --> 00:13:17.980
That's it!

00:13:18.330 --> 00:13:19.760
Blue mold!

00:13:19.760 --> 00:13:21.410
Penicillin!

00:13:21.410 --> 00:13:25.160
Penicillin is made from chrysogenum, 
a kind of blue mold!

00:13:25.160 --> 00:13:27.910
Sawaki, you can tell 
microbes apart, right?

00:13:28.260 --> 00:13:31.440
So you could raise pure cultures, right?

00:13:31.440 --> 00:13:32.910
I'm not really sure...

00:13:33.850 --> 00:13:35.940
I just grab one of these guys,

00:13:35.410 --> 00:13:37.420
P.   chrysogenum

00:13:35.940 --> 00:13:37.670
and put it in a petri dish 
or something, right?

00:13:38.050 --> 00:13:41.260
I can't see it, but yeah, 
that's the basic idea.

00:13:41.260 --> 00:13:45.520
Couldn't we sell pure strains of 
chrysogenum to labs and stuff?

00:13:45.520 --> 00:13:48.100
I'll go negotiate with 
the bio department!

00:13:48.100 --> 00:13:51.140
Tell them we can make 
100% pure cultures,

00:13:51.140 --> 00:13:53.080
but keep Sawaki's ability secret!

00:13:56.880 --> 00:13:58.000
Um...

00:13:58.660 --> 00:14:00.130
Does this mean I have

00:14:00.130 --> 00:14:02.300
to spend all my time 
collecting blue molds?

00:14:02.900 --> 00:14:04.580
I'm begging you!

00:14:05.410 --> 00:14:07.770
Think of our meeting as fate.

00:14:07.770 --> 00:14:10.320
The margin is all yours, of course.

00:14:10.840 --> 00:14:13.460
Margin... you mean money?

00:14:20.660 --> 00:14:23.850
The professor said there's 
enough blue mold in

00:14:23.850 --> 00:14:25.800
his own home to sell if he wanted to.

00:14:29.010 --> 00:14:30.550
I'm opening the window.

00:14:31.370 --> 00:14:33.290
Since it's come to this...

00:14:33.290 --> 00:14:36.860
You'll have to sell your giant 
stag beetles, Kawahama.

00:14:36.860 --> 00:14:38.820
I can't do that.

00:14:38.820 --> 00:14:41.420
They're my treasures.

00:14:42.960 --> 00:14:44.240
We have no choice!

00:14:44.240 --> 00:14:45.920
We've got to do something!

00:14:45.920 --> 00:14:49.960
Then spin some silk from the silkworms 
I gave you and sell that!

00:14:49.450 --> 00:14:54.450
Silkworms

00:14:49.960 --> 00:14:51.240
You mean these?!

00:14:51.240 --> 00:14:53.130
These "silkworms" you gave me?!

00:14:53.130 --> 00:14:55.250
They turned out to be just moths!

00:14:55.250 --> 00:14:56.720
And they're already dead!

00:14:56.720 --> 00:14:57.330
What?!

00:14:57.330 --> 00:14:59.630
What are you gonna do?! 
We're out of options!

00:14:59.630 --> 00:15:00.960
Shut up! I know that!

00:15:03.170 --> 00:15:04.490
Caterpillar fungus!

00:15:05.520 --> 00:15:06.710
Caterpillar fungus?

00:15:06.710 --> 00:15:08.030
You mean the stuff they

00:15:08.030 --> 00:15:10.010
call a secret elixir for 
eternal youth in China?

00:15:10.860 --> 00:15:13.650
They're all dead and being 
eaten by putrefying bacteria,

00:15:13.010 --> 00:15:16.010
C.   sinensis

00:15:13.010 --> 00:15:16.010
Putrefying 
Bacteria

00:15:13.650 --> 00:15:16.680
but one of them is covered 
in caterpillar fungus.

00:15:17.290 --> 00:15:19.740
They all look the same to me...

00:15:20.460 --> 00:15:22.440
But how did you know about that?

00:15:22.860 --> 00:15:25.940
You remember that lady, 
Sekiguchi, who lived by the bridge?

00:15:25.940 --> 00:15:31.650
Caterpillar Fungus

00:15:26.560 --> 00:15:29.000
She always bought it through mail order.

00:15:29.000 --> 00:15:31.650
She said a really small 
box cost twenty grand.

00:15:32.080 --> 00:15:33.410
Twenty grand?!

00:15:33.410 --> 00:15:36.910
They're hard to find in nature, 
so they're pretty valuable.

00:15:36.910 --> 00:15:38.180
Couldn't you cultivate these

00:15:38.180 --> 00:15:39.910
and sell them as herbal medicine?

00:15:39.910 --> 00:15:40.960
Are you serious?!

00:15:40.960 --> 00:15:43.120
Sawaki, we beg you! Help us!

00:15:43.120 --> 00:15:45.140
Sure, I could handle this.

00:15:45.140 --> 00:15:45.960
You mean it?!

00:15:46.290 --> 00:15:47.240
Sure.

00:15:47.240 --> 00:15:49.210
Caterpillar fungus, eh?

00:15:49.210 --> 00:15:50.760
All right!

00:15:50.760 --> 00:15:52.780
We might just make it after all!

00:15:52.780 --> 00:15:54.640
Tonight, we celebrate!

00:15:55.130 --> 00:15:56.720
Sawaki, are you sure?

00:15:57.210 --> 00:15:59.220
Well, I've never seen

00:15:59.220 --> 00:16:01.330
anyone so happy that I can see microbes.

00:16:01.940 --> 00:16:05.280
It sort of makes me happy 
to be relied upon.

00:16:01.940 --> 00:16:10.740
Banzai! Banzai! Banzai!

00:16:09.540 --> 00:16:10.740
I guess so.

00:16:15.160 --> 00:16:17.280
Oh, that's too bad.

00:16:17.830 --> 00:16:19.770
Sawaki-kun's ability is no more

00:16:19.770 --> 00:16:22.770
than a money-making 
tool to those two, eh?

00:16:23.940 --> 00:16:26.520
If that's the case, I have an idea, too.

00:16:27.000 --> 00:16:30.250
Estimate 
Enclosed

00:16:30.610 --> 00:16:33.420
If a student had to pay this amount,

00:16:33.420 --> 00:16:35.320
it would make things difficult...

00:16:35.320 --> 00:16:37.010
Cheers!

00:16:37.010 --> 00:16:40.970
Silkworms

00:16:41.980 --> 00:16:44.480
Are you heading home, 
too, Hasegawa-kun?

00:16:44.500 --> 00:16:47.340
Notice: The following students, please report to Professor Itsuki's lab today at 10:00.
First year: Sawaki Tadayasu  
First year: Yuuki Kei  
Second year: Kawahama Takuma  
Second year: Misato Kaoru
You'll regret it if you don't come. -Itsuki

00:16:44.940 --> 00:16:47.360
No, there's still some 
data I want to work on.

00:16:47.780 --> 00:16:51.860
Oh? Well, just make sure 
you're free by tomorrow.

00:16:51.860 --> 00:16:52.900
Bye.

00:17:06.920 --> 00:17:09.100
Ugh... it's dark already.

00:17:11.090 --> 00:17:12.300
You're awake?

00:17:12.800 --> 00:17:15.630
I'm going to Professor 
Itsuki's lab for a bit.

00:17:16.100 --> 00:17:17.760
We left our bags there, and all.

00:17:17.760 --> 00:17:19.690
Couldn't we go tomorrow?

00:17:19.690 --> 00:17:21.460
Well, they're asleep anyway.

00:17:21.460 --> 00:17:22.520
It seemed like a good chance.

00:17:23.080 --> 00:17:24.180
I'll be right back.

00:17:34.670 --> 00:17:38.710
These guys didn't test 
me like Professor Itsuki

00:17:38.710 --> 00:17:40.640
and Hasegawa-san did.

00:17:43.330 --> 00:17:45.170
Most people would be 
disgusted, freaked out,

00:17:45.170 --> 00:17:46.460
or just not believe me.

00:17:47.570 --> 00:17:49.860
Teacher, Sawaki-kun is weird!

00:17:49.860 --> 00:17:52.610
He says he can see stuff 
that none of us can see!

00:17:52.610 --> 00:17:53.840
It's so gross!

00:17:54.240 --> 00:17:57.920
Sawaki-san's boy, Tadayasu, 
is a bit strange, isn't he?

00:17:57.920 --> 00:18:02.010
It's normal for kids to say all 
kinds of things for attention.

00:18:02.810 --> 00:18:04.580
Seeing microbes...

00:18:04.580 --> 00:18:06.930
If you don't want to eat it, just say so.

00:18:06.930 --> 00:18:08.440
Why do you have to tell lies?

00:18:09.140 --> 00:18:10.630
What's wrong, Tadayasu?

00:18:10.630 --> 00:18:12.690
Eat and feel better!

00:18:13.510 --> 00:18:15.150
What's wrong, Tadayasu?

00:18:19.340 --> 00:18:21.410
Hang on! We'll get blown away!

00:18:30.510 --> 00:18:32.830
I guess I'll play with them. 
It has been a while.

00:18:38.670 --> 00:18:40.890
Green, come to this one.

00:18:42.250 --> 00:18:44.960
The rice balls can be a palette 
for the yellow molds.

00:18:49.710 --> 00:18:50.980
Pardon me.

00:18:51.860 --> 00:18:53.770
Well, if it isn't Sawaki's other half.

00:18:54.490 --> 00:18:56.120
You were still on campus?

00:18:56.120 --> 00:18:58.280
Yeah, in those two second-years' dorm.

00:18:59.120 --> 00:19:00.200
I see.

00:19:00.200 --> 00:19:02.990
Sorry to interrupt. We forgot our bags.

00:19:02.990 --> 00:19:04.950
Sure, they're right there.

00:19:05.270 --> 00:19:06.200
Thanks.

00:19:10.230 --> 00:19:12.070
It must be hard on you, too.

00:19:13.360 --> 00:19:16.590
How do you plan to stay 
with Sawaki from now on?

00:19:16.980 --> 00:19:18.320
How...

00:19:18.710 --> 00:19:20.620
It's not a problem at all.

00:19:21.130 --> 00:19:23.240
We're the sons of families who own 
a brewery and a mold-starter business,

00:19:23.240 --> 00:19:24.890
so we'll probably always be...

00:19:24.890 --> 00:19:26.530
That's not what I meant.

00:19:28.330 --> 00:19:30.480
I'll give you a friendly warning.

00:19:31.680 --> 00:19:34.640
If you consider his 
ability to see microbes

00:19:34.640 --> 00:19:36.740
in terms of a complete set

00:19:36.740 --> 00:19:38.980
of transmission electron microscopes,

00:19:38.980 --> 00:19:40.320
he's worth 300 million yen.

00:19:40.980 --> 00:19:43.450
300 million? No way.

00:19:44.280 --> 00:19:46.810
If word of his ability got out,

00:19:46.810 --> 00:19:48.660
Professor Itsuki, Whiskers, and Fatso

00:19:48.660 --> 00:19:51.460
wouldn't be the only ones trying 
to take advantage of it.

00:21:24.970 --> 00:21:27.470
Moyashimon

00:21:24.970 --> 00:21:27.470
Episode 2

00:21:25.630 --> 00:21:27.470
Microbe Theater

00:21:26.030 --> 00:21:27.470
Microbe Theater 2!

00:21:32.140 --> 00:21:34.140
Chrysogenum  
Blue Mold

00:21:32.680 --> 00:21:36.230
I'm Chrysogenum, 
also known as blue mold.

00:21:37.770 --> 00:21:39.300
We love humidity!

00:21:39.300 --> 00:21:40.790
Love it!

00:21:45.610 --> 00:21:47.290
Who are you?

00:21:47.150 --> 00:21:51.240
Tricoides

00:21:47.290 --> 00:21:49.070
I'm Tricoides.

00:21:49.070 --> 00:21:51.240
We live between your bathroom tiles.

00:21:51.440 --> 00:21:53.500
We're the black-ish spots!

00:21:53.500 --> 00:21:55.960
That's why they call us black mold!

00:21:54.250 --> 00:21:55.960
Black Mold

00:21:56.590 --> 00:21:57.540
Wow!

00:21:57.540 --> 00:21:58.300
Whoa!

00:21:58.300 --> 00:21:58.940
Hi!

00:21:58.940 --> 00:21:59.630
Hi!

00:21:59.630 --> 00:22:00.510
Hi!

00:22:00.510 --> 00:22:02.290
Wow, you sure are lively.

00:22:02.290 --> 00:22:03.810
Who are you?

00:22:02.960 --> 00:22:06.550
Alternata  Soot Mold

00:22:03.810 --> 00:22:07.010
I'm Alternata, also known as soot mold.

00:22:07.010 --> 00:22:08.630
If you're not careful, we can

00:22:08.630 --> 00:22:10.540
even brew in your contact lens solution.

00:22:10.540 --> 00:22:12.730
We also live deep inside 
air conditioners.

00:22:12.730 --> 00:22:14.090
We're all molds!

00:22:14.090 --> 00:22:14.950
Yep, all molds.

00:22:14.950 --> 00:22:16.990
We're molds! Shut up, you little molds!

00:22:16.990 --> 00:22:18.220
Yeah!

00:22:19.630 --> 00:22:22.480
There's nothing but mold in this room...

00:22:23.240 --> 00:22:24.940
What a great room.

00:22:24.960 --> 00:22:31.200
In Microbe Theater 
Episode 3,

00:22:24.960 --> 00:22:31.200
We'll Do the Brewing.

00:22:31.200 --> 00:22:59.980
Next Week: 
"The Microbes Are Gonna Brew!"

00:22:31.590 --> 00:22:35.540
So, have you heard of hongeohoe?
